policy_facts:
Nothing new is sent or kept: the re-ask list now says exactly what the code at 88e1c84d already does (l6words#4). A box the Cardano server hasn't answered for is asked about again at each later pool read that counts your boxes:
- opening or refreshing Lovejoin's page;
- the page's read again after each thing you do there, or as a run bringing every box back that it shows ends;
- pressing a Bring one back button;
- the wallet's own reads at each unlock and as boxes come back on their schedule;
- the read after Bring every box back now or Bring every box in this pool back now stops (2 hours on, if it sent anything), or after the retired pools' run ends.
Those runs' own pool reads, and Pay from my private balance anyway's, ask nothing.

The merge rule as round seven builds it (R7-code's change to what gets spent together):
- a token pool's way back is counted by what it pays beside the change a spend leaves you anyway;
- boxes still come after your other money where one transaction can't spend all of it, so a session's funding takes another session's money before a box where that pays;
- none of it refuses, or sends in parts, a spend the wallet would otherwise send as one transaction: where none of the rule's choices can go, it falls back to those.
